          "0": {
            "id": "13998246",
            "headline": "SEBI approves IPO proposals of Jakson Green, SNVA Traveltech, Playsimple Games and six others",
            "heading": "SEBI approves IPO proposals of Jakson Green, SNVA Traveltech, Playsimple Games and six others",
            "intro": "Upcoming IPOs | SEBI issued its observations on the IPO papers of Laxyo on August 3, Rediff on August 4, and Garuda Aerospace on August 5. Further, the capital markets regulator issued its observations on the draft documents of Jakson Green, SNVA Traveltech, and Playsimple Games on August 6.",
            "body": "Jakson Green, Rediff.com India, SNVA Traveltech and Playsimple Games are among nine companies that have received approval from the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) to proceed with their initial public offerings (IPOs).\r\n\r\nThe capital markets regulator has also cleared the IPO proposals of Expression 360 Services India, Adroit Industries India, Garuda Aerospace, Naini Papers and Laxyo.\r\n\r\nGreen energy transition platform Jakson Green filed its draft papers through the confidential route in December 2025. AvenuesAI subsidiary Rediff.com India and Travomint platform operator SNVA Traveltech also filed confidential draft papers in March 2026. Drone maker Garuda Aerospace and paper manufacturer Naini Papers opted for the confidential filing route in April 2026.\r\n\r\nAdvertising services provider Expression 360 Services India and automotive components manufacturer Adroit Industries India filed their draft red herring prospectuses (DRHPs) with SEBI in March this year, while Bengaluru-based mobile gaming company Playsimple Games submitted its draft papers in April.\r\n\r\nSEBI issued its observations on Laxyo's draft papers on August 3, followed by Rediff.com India on August 4 and Garuda Aerospace on August 5. Jakson Green, SNVA Traveltech and Playsimple Games received the regulator's observations on August 6, while Expression 360 Services India, Adroit Industries India and Naini Papers secured the approval on August 7.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nThe issuance of SEBI observations indicates that the companies have received the regulator's approval to launch their IPOs. The approval remains valid for one year, during which the companies can tap the capital markets.\r\n\r\nHowever, companies that have filed their draft papers through the confidential route have up to 18 months to launch their IPOs.\r\n\r\nRenewable green energy company Jakson Green is reportedly planning to raise around Rs 2,000 crore, while reports indicated that the media company Rediff.com India, the subsidiary of fintech firm AvenuesAI, is looking to tap capital markets for Rs 600-800 crore fundraise for repositioning from a legacy Internet portal to an AI-led digital platform.\r\n\r\nThe amount SNVA Traveltech, the Noida-based operator of online travel platform Travomint that offers technology-driven travel solutions to customers worldwide, and paper products maker Naini Papers plan to raise through their IPOs is not known.\r\n\r\nPlaysimple Games, which claims to be the largest Indian pure-play casual mobile gaming company, intends to raise up to Rs 3,150 crore through its initial public offering (IPO), comprising entirely an offer-for-sale (OFS) by its existing promoter, MTGx Gaming Holding AB, which currently holds more than a 97 percent stake in the company.\r\n\r\nKolkata-based advertising and media company Expression 360 Services India also proposed to raise funds entirely through an offer-for-sale of 1.5 crore equity shares. Promoter Mohit Gupta will offload shares in the OFS.\r\n\r\nGaruda Aerospace, the Chennai-based drone technology company, is reportedly planning to raise around Rs 1,000 crore through its IPO, comprising a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 750 crore and an offer-for-sale (OFS) worth Rs 250 crore.\r\n\r\nMadhya Pradesh-based Adroit Industries, a manufacturer and supplier of propeller shafts and related torque-transmission components for the automotive and non-automotive industries, has proposed to raise funds through an IPO of 1.12 crore equity shares. The public issue comprises a fresh issue of 98.97 lakh shares alongside an offer-for-sale of 13.5 lakh shares by a promoter.\r\n\r\nAdroit intends to utilise the net proceeds from the fresh issue to procure machinery and equipment to enhance operations at its Dewas and Pithampur facilities, as well as transportation vehicles for the movement of goods between the manufacturing units. The funds will also be used to repay debt at its subsidiary, Adroit Driveshafts, while the remaining amount will be allocated toward general corporate purposes.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/jakson-green-rediff-snva-traveltech-playsimple-games-among-9-ipos-received-sebi-nod-13998246.html",
            "ai_impact_text_option_s": "Bullet",
